5.3 Outflow Limitation Impact Factors




                    模
     In addition to the effects of total basin supply and water levels, other weather variations
and meteorological conditions can limit outflow from dams, with the main considerations in




                  学
our outflow model being rainfall over the coming period of time, a dramatic increase in the
flow of the Ottawa River due to winter snowpack melt in the spring and ice jams on the river




                 数
in the winter, as well as natural factors such as winds on the lake.

