6.3 Optimal water-level determination model based on NSGA-II algorithm




                    模
     NSGA-II (Non-dominated Sorting Genetic Algorithm II) is a genetic algorithm for solving
multi-objective optimization problems. It finds the Pareto optimal solution by iterating.




                  学
     1. Coding and initializing populations
     First, the solution to the problem is encoded by using the binary operation. Each individual




                 数
in the population represents a set of possible solutions, i.e., a set of values for water level (H)
and water flow (Q). For each individual, the values of water level (H) and water flow (Q) can
              ：
be generated randomly within a given constraint. Combined with the complexity of this prob-




             els
lem, we chose an initial population size of 100 individuals.
            号
     2. Calculating Adaptation



           od
     NSGA-II is a minimization problem solver, so we take the negative of these objective
         众


functions as the fitness function.
        Hm
     3. Undominated sorting and congestion calculation
       公



     The NSGA-II algorithm will rank and select individuals in the population based on non-
dominated ordering and crowding. Undominated ordering divides the population into multiple
     AT
     信




ranked frontiers, each containing individuals who are not dominated by each other.
     The crowding degree comparison is used to differentiate between individuals within the
   微




same frontier, giving preference to individuals with lower crowding degrees (i.e., fewer neigh-
   M



bors around them) in order to maintain the diversity of the solution.
 ：




     4. Selection, crossover, and mutation
     The selection operation is based on the tournament selection method, where parent indi-
号




viduals are selected for crossover and mutation to produce a new generation of individuals.

     5. Generation of new populations
   信




     Combining parents and offspring, new populations are selected by non-dominated sorting
and crowding calculations.
  微




     6. Iterating until the termination condition is met
     The above steps are repeated until a predetermined number of iterations is reached or the
quality of the solution is no longer significantly improved.
     Based on the above calculation process, R studio is used to solve equation (34) and used

